      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T08:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we understood the concerns. The fact that the upper-constraint bump (7.1) happened so late was quite unfortunate. We probably need some process change, practically that FF of python-openstackclient should happen at the same time as Oslo libs.\nNevertheless, I\u0027m supporting @stephenfin@redhat.com \u0027s approach to allow this patch to bump upper constraints as soon as possible as it *looks like* not that risky and could spare us unnecessary churns and pain. @dms@danplanet.com, can you please remove your -1 to speed up this thing and let the problem solve itself as soon as possible? Thanks in advnace.",
      "parentUuid": "0a15e5e7_afd94520",
      "revId": "139b63c77cf4f1343298699c4648157f0a1fbf8a",
